- **Still missing:** the issue has no link to that pipeline. The looper can't look it up either, because it still has no access to GitLab project 88513714 (the API returns 404).
- **What I did:** I commented on the issue, put the `needs-decision` label back so it isn't re-run with nothing to act on, and saved a checkpoint. The checkpoint pushed only the run's own log and prompt files to `looper/cloud-77`; there were no code changes.

When the hub posts the pipeline's URL, the next run will wait on it and close the issue if it's green, or fix the cause if it's red.
